column5:
ped; I didn't test "plus" but it should hurt).  The theme signal c_i is item-specific and NOT captured by any mean. So no mean or fixed vector can boost it. Confirmed.  Therefore 0.50 requires item-dependent nonlinear steering, which requires a function-vector-like mechanism that triggers the model's OWN theme-extraction computation. My theme-FV attempt failed, possibly due to poor construction.  Let me make ONE more careful FV attempt, then finalize regardless.  Better FV construction (following the paper §2.1 "motivating observation" exactly): - Task: "scene → theme". - ICL prompts: "Scene: {s1}
Theme: {t1}
Scene: {s2}
Theme: {t2}
...
Scene: {sN}
Theme:" (N exemplars + empty answer slot).
